From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 08:21:07 -0400
Subject: switcher: Ctrl-Tab through the Space's recent tabs, a hold-to-see
 strip, folder-aware row moves

SpaceModel keeps an activation history per Space (docs/features/switcher.md
X1); Ctrl-Tab and Ctrl-Shift-Tab walk the five most recent tabs of the
active Space through spaces::CycleRecentTab, ahead of Chromium's kCtrlTabMru,
which stays off. A tap is one step (X2). Ctrl held past 150 ms shows a strip
over the page -- a layered child of the BrowserView with favicon, title and
the Space's colour per cell, the position highlighted; releasing Ctrl
commits the run, Escape cancels it, a mouse press or a key without Ctrl
commits (X3). Option-Shift-Cmd-Down / Up move the row within its container:
a row inside a folder stays inside, a folder beside a row is jumped as one
row, and moves that touch no folder keep Chromium's group rules (X4). The
setting stedding.tabs.ctrl_tab_mru returns Ctrl-Tab to strip order when off
(X5). The recent list counts a split once (splits J2). The shortcut
reference lists the chords and the divergence; the bar's actions mode gains
"Go to the Most Recent Tab".

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 2 (R6-12), Arc's Ctrl-Tab and its travel keys.
Removable when: Chromium's Ctrl-Tab MRU is scoped to a window's visible tabs
and shows a strip, and its relative tab move understands folders.
